Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 21:35:40 +0800
Subject: rewind: restore deduplicated files when rolling back older snapshots

- restore_snapshot now resolves manifest entries without a physical copy
  by walking back through the incremental chain to the newest snapshot
  that holds the file, so restoring an older snapshot no longer leaves
  deduplicated files at their current content.
- A size check guards the chain lookup, and when no copy exists anywhere
  the restore fails with the missing paths listed instead of silently
  succeeding with a partial restore.
- take_snapshot removes the partially written snapshot directory when
  the walk or manifest write fails, and list_snapshots skips directories
  without a manifest instead of showing blank picker entries.
- Adds regression tests for middle-snapshot restore, corrupt chains,
  and manifest-less snapshot directories.
